From 764a5bb25ec3e18bae869e6fef39fca0fa8af851 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rehanraza786 <rehanraza786@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:04:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] Insights: stamp provenance, bound volume, clamp what
 reaches context
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Making docs/insights.json committed also makes it attacker-controlled in
any repo that takes PRs, and an insight is free prose fed straight into an
agent's orientation — a more steerable channel than an assertion (a
structured edge) or an ADR (visibly a document). Three consequences, all
closed here.

Provenance is the indexer's, not the file's. The ingest previously copied
the model field verbatim and explain rendered it, so an entry could write
model:"ariadne-parser" and be displayed as a parsed fact — breaking the
invariant that a derived fact is never mistaken for a parsed one. Rows
loaded from a file are now stamped source='file' (new column, migrated in
place), the model string is clamped to a display-safe token, and explain
reports the stamp rather than the claim. Live writers stamp source='live'.

Volume is bounded. A single commit could previously add unlimited entries;
ingest now caps at maxInsights (default 2000, .ariadne/config.json) and
warns on the remainder.

context_pack stays near its advertised size. It carries at most one
insight (LIMIT 1, so it is flat in insight count) but emitted it
untruncated, and summaries run to 4000 chars — a 4x blowup of a pack that
documents itself as ~900 bytes. Both editions now clamp to
maxInsightChars (default 600) and point at explain for the full text.

Both knobs are documented in SETUP.md and README.md alongside the existing
context-budget settings.

The residual control on all of this is human review, so the
graph-augmentation skill now says what reviewing these files actually
requires: read an insight summary as an instruction to a machine rather
than as documentation, check an assertion's evidence chain rather than its
conclusion, and treat bulk additions as a question. Nothing downstream
re-checks a merged entry.

PRIVACY.md's storage table said insights are local and uncommitted. That
is no longer true: they are committed, versioned, and published in the CI
index artifact. Corrected, with the tradeoff stated plainly and the
opt-out described.

run_tests.py: a committed insight cannot forge parser provenance.
